{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ribbonlike-effective-meadowlark","creation_channel":"python","description":"# Fix f449 ADR citation for unbounded Jira DC reindex support\n\n## Problem\nThe f449 ticket description and `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` module docstring cite \"ADR 0037 s3\" for the unbounded Jira DC reindex behavior, but ADR 0037 is `oss-contribution-intake-posture`. The cited support lives in `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` around line 282.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The f449-era description/docstring reference no longer points readers to ADR 0037 for Jira DC reindex behavior.\n- [ ] `snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` cites `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` (or ADR 0055) for the Jira-family sub-seam/reindex support.\n- [ ] Any related documentation wording remains consistent with the actual ADR titles and section content.\n","id":"3e03-786b-cdc7-460b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Fix f449 ADR citation for unbounded Jira DC reindex support"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788288573500695001,"uuid":"22d994fb-ceb0-4963-a0c2-e1dae12f5a8a"}